[D] D_inf and why it constrains nothing  (task 3)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 D_inf := exp sum_{alpha>=0} (1-alpha) A(alpha)    (RS2:35, X01:67)  -- a VALUE
 lambda_Ur := limsup |phi^U|^{1/n}                                  -- a RADIUS
   U=0.25  (in KP window)   D_inf(geom closed form) = 1.344868577
   U=0.5654 (beta=1/12)     D_inf(geom closed form) = 0.4061889168
   U=33.9785 (beta=2.5)     D_inf(geom closed form) = 1.06548684
   reproduce corpus: D_inf(0.25) = 1.34487  ->  1.34486857738

 *and the closed form is NOT a sum at U>1 (TT1:125): radius 1, series diverges.
  continuation value at U=33.9785 is 1.0654868 > 0 but meaningless -- it is exp(complex-free
  analytic continuation of a divergent series), NOT evidence about D_inf(2.5).

 SCALE INVARIANCE WITNESS (why D_inf cannot bound lambda_Ur in EITHER direction):
  rescale every cluster weight: A(alpha) -> c*A(alpha).
    * lambda_Ur -> c^{1/n} growth ... careful: lambda_Ur is defined from |phi^U|,
      so c*|phi^U| gives lambda_Ur -> c*lambda_Ur.  Instead use the RATIO-FREE test:
      adding a term only at alpha=0,1 changes D_inf arbitrarily, changes limsup not at all.
     spike A(0) += 0.0    : log D_inf = 0.2962962963   (was 0.2962963) ; limsup |A|^{1/n} unchanged
     spike A(0) += 1.0    : log D_inf = 1.296296296    (was 0.2962963) ; limsup |A|^{1/n} unchanged
     spike A(0) += 5.0    : log D_inf = 5.296296296    (was 0.2962963) ; limsup |A|^{1/n} unchanged
     spike A(0) += -3.0   : log D_inf = -2.703703704   (was 0.2962963) ; limsup |A|^{1/n} unchanged
  => D_inf and lambda_Ur are independent functionals of {A(alpha)}.
  => D_inf(0.25)=1.34487 => f1^2 = a0*D_inf > a0  [T] , but ZERO constraint on lambda_Ur.
     (Also: 1.34487 is a geometric-model value at U=0.25, deep inside the window,
      not a value at beta=2.5 at all.)

